      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5d29fed11c6de66cbecd1d4a|full_name}: Index controllers override all hand gesture animations. If you do, say, rockandroll with the index controller and the rockandroll animation makes the avatar flip the bird, it will only flip the bird if you're using anything but the index controllers.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-10-24T14:35:13.818Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Currently when we have all our fingers extended with the Index controllers our avatars do this ✋. The open hand gesture seems to activate even before we fully extend our fingers, which is good, don't change that. What I'd like is once we have all our fingers completely straight (no curl) our avatars should do this 🖐️. If we want to do this ✋ then we could just put our thumb down.\n\nThis would be a welcome QOL change for people who use Index controllers and want that extra immersion since to make the open hand gesture index users do this 🖐️ in real life and non-index users' avatars do this 🖐️ for open hand so why should Index users be limited from this?",
